# Gate step 1211-q9bm — data, not code.
#
# Binds the completion-time refusal for plan/long-running.md. Hermetic: every arm
# builds a throwaway plan/ tree and runs the binary there, so no arm writes a
# fragment into this checkout or reads its real view.
#
# WHY THE REFUSAL MOVED. check-long-running-view.sh is correct and stays — but it
# runs inside the GATE, so a stale row is paid for by whoever lands NEXT rather
# than by whoever created it. Measured 2026-09-15: completing 330 left its row
# behind and blocked landing fleet-wide; yoga had to prove the refusal was not
# theirs, find the owner, and decide whether editing another host's lane was
# acceptable. The author never saw it. The checker's own message already names
# the right moment — "in the same commit as the change that moved it" — which is
# a completion-time instruction delivered at land time to a different person.
#
# THE ARMS THAT MATTER ARE THE NEGATIVE CONTROLS (2, 3, 4). This guard must fire
# ONLY on the exact stranding condition: a row already absent, a packet that is
# not multi_cycle, or a non-terminal flip must all pass untouched, or it becomes
# a tax on every closure in the fleet and on the in_progress flips a multi_cycle
# packet makes between cycles. Arm 5 pins that the LAND-TIME CHECK REMAINS — this
# is an early courtesy to the author and cannot see a flip that bypasses
# set-field, so removing the backstop would trade a late refusal for none.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking a terminal flip that would strand the long-running view is refused at the flip (1211-q9bm)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-long-running-view-refuses-at-completion.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the completion-time refusal for plan/long-running.md regressed (1211-q9bm) — either a terminal flip can again strand the view (so the next host to land pays for it), or the guard has widened and is refusing closures it should not: a non-multi_cycle packet, a row already removed, or the in_progress flip a multi_cycle packet makes every cycle; see the failing arm above"
STEP_OK="long-running view completion-time refusal check passed"
# Exit 3 means no plan binary was resolvable — nothing was exercised, and the
# fixture says so by name rather than passing.
STEP_SKIP_EXIT=3
STEP_SKIP_DESC="no tillandsias-plan binary resolved, so the refusal could not be exercised"
